-- title:
--   A-section through a non-crossing point of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$, and assume every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is trivial already lies in $H$, with $M/p$ non-zero. Let `hj` record that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of properties and data for the two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over `R p`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : \mathrm{R}\,p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map. Let $i \in \{0,1\}$ and let $P_0$ be a closed point of the curve $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ attached to these data, and write $x$ for the image of $P_0$ under the map on points of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ followed by the $i$-th component map $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,i$ into the fibre `fibre ((residue A).comp ρ)`. Assume $x$ lies outside the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,j$ for every $j \ne i$. Then there exist: a section $y$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; a morphism $u : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to$ `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over $\mathrm{Spec}(\rho)$; an identification of the restriction of $u$ along $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $y$ composed with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection; and a morphism $u_\kappa$ from $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$ to `fibre ((residue A).comp ρ)` whose first projection is the reduction of $u$ and whose second projection is the identity, such that $x$ is the image of the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$ under $u_\kappa$.
--
--   This is the lifting step for the Deligne–Rapoport model at a level exactly divisible by $p$: a closed point of the special fibre lying on only one of the two components is the special point of a section over the valuation ring $A$, whose generic point is a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of the curve. It is used in the analysis of which points of the special fibre come from prolongation data, in the study of the reduction of $X_H(M)$ at $p$.
